% Lesson 23, exercise 2: intervals stated outright, as an HR system
% stores them, guarded by integrity constraints.
%
%   python3 datalog.py exercises/23-answers.dl      (exits 3: two violations)

%        person  employer  from          until (exclusive)
employed(ann,    acme,     "2020-01-01", "2021-06-30").
employed(ann,    globex,   "2021-06-01", "9999-12-31").   % a month too early
employed(ben,    initech,  "2022-03-01", "2022-02-01").   % typed backwards
employed(cy,     acme,     "2019-01-01", "2020-01-01").
employed(cy,     acme,     "2020-01-01", "2023-01-01").   % adjacent: fine

% A period may not close before it opens (or on the day it opens).
:- employed(P, C, F, U), U <= F.

% Nobody has two employers at once.  C1 < C2 reports each pair once,
% and leaves two periods at the same employer alone.
:- employed(P, C1, F1, U1), employed(P, C2, F2, U2), C1 < C2,
   F1 < U2, F2 < U1.
